# Local-dev path overrides — copy to .cargo/config.toml (untracked) to iterate against
# sibling checkouts instead of the rev/tag pins in Cargo.toml.
#
#   cp .cargo/config.toml.example .cargo/config.toml
#
# Why it lives HERE and not in Cargo.toml: a [patch] in the manifest is committed, so it
# ships to every consumer and every deploy image, and the "works on my laptop" build stops
# matching the deployed one. That mismatch is what this extraction exists to remove — the
# lodedb pin drifted exactly this way (manifest said v2.0.2, the sibling patch silently
# built v2.0.3). Cargo reads [patch] from config.toml the same as from a manifest, so this
# gives the same fast iteration with none of the reach.
#
# Adjust the paths to wherever you keep the sibling repos.

# core resolves lodedb-core from the public tag (v2.0.2, ae5ac18; O-41) and arc's relay
# by path (5f5a734); add a [patch] here only to iterate against a sibling checkout.
